---
title: "member_profile_update (stem-system: Clubhouse Manager)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_check_session: server action invoked
    q_check_session --> q_error_unauth: no authenticated session
    q_check_session --> q_validate_input: session valid
    q_error_unauth --> [*]: return error
    q_validate_input --> q_error_validation: zod validation fails
    q_validate_input --> q_check_permission: input valid
    q_error_validation --> [*]: return validation error
    q_check_permission --> q_update_own: user is updating own profile (target_id == session.user.id)
    q_check_permission --> q_check_admin: user is updating another profile
    q_check_admin --> q_error_forbidden: user is not admin (is_admin != true)
    q_check_admin --> q_update_other: user is admin
    q_error_forbidden --> [*]: return 403 forbidden
    q_update_own --> q_db_update: update member record (RLS client, own row only)
    q_update_other --> q_db_update_admin: update member record (admin client, bypass RLS)
    q_db_update --> q_sync_discord: fire-and-forget nickname update via Discord bot
    q_db_update_admin --> q_sync_discord: fire-and-forget nickname update via Discord bot
    q_sync_discord --> [*]: return success, revalidatePath

    note right of q_check_permission
        INV-001: non-admin users can only update their own profile
        INV-002: admin check queries members table for is_admin = true
    end note

    note right of q_db_update
        INV-003: RLS client ensures user can only modify own row
        INV-004: admin client bypasses RLS (required for cross-user updates)
    end note

    note right of q_sync_discord
        INV-005: Discord sync errors are logged but do not fail the mutation
    end note
